      "math_academy_id": "e-3976",
      "problem": "Express $7^0 = 1$ in logarithmic form.",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a = b^x$ is equivalent to $\\log_{b}{a} = x$\n\nIf we compare $7^0 = 1$ with $a = b^x,$ we get $a = 1, b = 7,$ and $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the equation $7^0 = 1$ is equivalent to $\\log_{7}{1}= 0.$\n\nIn general, $\\log_n(1) = 0$ for any $n>0, n\\neq 1.$",
